---
import Base from '../layouts/Base.astro';
---
<Base title="Science communications" description="Children's books, podcasts, and press pieces by Aiyu Zheng that bring ecology to wider audiences.">
  <div class="wrap">
    <div class="page-title">
      <h1>Science communications</h1>
      <p class="lede">Bringing ecology to readers and listeners outside the university, in Chinese and English.</p>
    </div>

    <section class="section split">
      <div>
        <p class="eyebrow">Merging art and science education</p>
        <h2>Children’s books</h2>
        <p>I illustrated and wrote a series of children’s books to introduce young children to the ecology of herbs widely used in Chinese medicine and culture.</p>
        <div class="entry-list">
          <p><a href="https://www.amazon.com/%E5%86%AC%E8%99%AB%E5%A4%8F%E8%8D%89%E7%9A%84%E6%97%85%E9%80%94-%E5%A5%87%E5%A6%99%E7%9A%84%E6%9C%AC%E8%8D%89-%E9%83%91%E8%89%BE%E9%9B%A8/dp/7534799759/" target="_blank" rel="noopener">The Journey of <em>Ophiocordyceps sinensis</em> (<em>in Chinese</em>) (2019). Central China Media. ISBN 978-7-5347-9975-4.</a></p>
          <p><a href="https://www.amazon.com/Mini-Paradise-Lotus-Chinese/dp/7571101670" target="_blank" rel="noopener">The Mini Paradise of the Lotus (<em>in Chinese</em>) (2019). Central China Media. ISBN 978-7-5711-0167-1.</a></p>
        </div>
      </div>
      <div class="covers">
        <img src="/uploads/2023/10/JPEG-image-1882056FB4AD-1-2.jpeg" alt="Cover of The Journey of Ophiocordyceps sinensis" loading="lazy" />
        <img src="/uploads/2023/10/JPEG-image-F3D335CFAB77-1-2-1.jpeg" alt="Cover of The Mini Paradise of the Lotus" loading="lazy" />
      </div>
    </section>

    <section class="section split" style="grid-template-columns: 1fr 2fr;">
      <figure style="margin:0">
        <a href="https://podcasts.apple.com/us/podcast/%E8%8A%B1%E9%97%B4%E6%9C%89%E5%89%91%E5%AE%A2/id1553544664" target="_blank" rel="noopener" style="border:0"><img class="rounded" src="/uploads/2023/10/Screen-Shot-2023-10-10-at-10.51.51-PM.png" alt="rosesNswords podcast cover" loading="lazy" /></a>
        <figcaption><a href="https://podcasts.apple.com/us/podcast/%E8%8A%B1%E9%97%B4%E6%9C%89%E5%89%91%E5%AE%A2/id1553544664" target="_blank" rel="noopener">rosesNswords 花间有剑客</a></figcaption>
      </figure>
      <div>
        <p class="eyebrow">Raising the voice of diversity and inclusion</p>
        <h2>Podcasts</h2>
        <p>I cohost a bilingual podcast with friends to communicate our science and experiences as female scientists in research and academia. I also do scientific outreach with other podcasts.</p>
        <div class="entry-list">
          <p>小红书的年轻人为啥都在树上？| 001 抱树 | about热水频道 <a href="https://podcasts.apple.com/cn/podcast/%E5%B0%8F%E7%BA%A2%E4%B9%A6%E4%B8%8A%E7%9A%84%E5%B9%B4%E8%BD%BB%E4%BA%BA%E4%B8%BA%E5%95%A5%E9%83%BD%E5%9C%A8%E6%A0%91%E4%B8%8A-001%E6%8A%B1%E6%A0%91/id1704592892?i=1000625883649" target="_blank" rel="noopener">“Why are young users of Chinese Instagram (<em>Xiaohongshu</em>) hugging trees?”</a> (<em>in Chinese</em>). Invited speaker at the podcast series <em>aboüt channel</em>. August 17, 2023. Apple Podcasts. We discussed how plants exhibit diverse strategies in a competitive environment and how humans can reconnect with nature by hugging trees.</p>
          <p>当极端天气不再极端罕见 | S1E9 | 花间有剑客 × 不成气候 <a href="https://podcasts.apple.com/us/podcast/s1-e9-%E8%87%AA%E7%84%B6%E5%8F%91%E5%A3%B0-%E8%8A%B1%E9%97%B4%E6%9C%89%E5%89%91%E5%AE%A2-x-%E4%B8%8D%E6%88%90%E6%B0%94%E5%80%99-%E5%BD%93%E6%9E%81%E7%AB%AF%E5%A4%A9%E6%B0%94%E4%B8%8D%E5%86%8D%E6%9E%81%E7%AB%AF%E7%BD%95%E8%A7%81/id1553544664?i=1000541044474" target="_blank" rel="noopener">“When extreme weather is not rare anymore.”</a> (<em>in Chinese</em>). Host at the podcast series <em>rosesNswords</em>. November 7, 2021. Apple Podcasts / Spotify. We introduced the patterns of extreme weather under climate change to the general audience.</p>
          <p>野地故事：揭开热带竹未解之谜的生态学日常 | S1E7 | 花间有剑客 <a href="https://podcasts.apple.com/us/podcast/s1-e7-%E8%87%AA%E7%84%B6%E5%8F%91%E5%A3%B0-%E9%87%8E%E5%9C%B0%E6%95%85%E4%BA%8B-%E6%8F%AD%E5%BC%80%E7%83%AD%E5%B8%A6%E7%AB%B9%E6%9C%AA%E8%A7%A3%E4%B9%8B%E8%B0%9C%E7%9A%84%E7%94%9F%E6%80%81%E5%AD%A6%E6%97%A5%E5%B8%B8/id1553544664?i=1000531977389" target="_blank" rel="noopener">“Unraveling the mysteries of tropical bamboos in the field.”</a> (<em>in Chinese</em>). Host at the podcast series <em>rosesNswords</em>. August 13, 2021. Apple Podcasts / Spotify. I introduced my research on tropical bamboos and why they are a mesmerizing group for ecological research.</p>
        </div>
      </div>
    </section>

    <section class="section split" style="grid-template-columns: 2fr 1fr;">
      <div>
        <p class="eyebrow">Making science accessible and fun</p>
        <h2>Press</h2>
        <p>I wrote science communication pieces for platforms targeting different readers, from students of ecology to entrepreneurs.</p>
        <div class="entry-list">
          <p>由性状演化追寻竹子的一生 | 小云杉LPICEA微信公众号 “Tracing the life of bamboo through its trait evolution.” (<em>in Chinese</em>). The Blog of Lab of Plant Interactions: Climate, Ecosystem, and Atmosphere at Tsinghua University, China. November 2023.</p>
          <p>森林的内卷与解法 | 小红书附属刊物 “The involution and evolution of forests.” Xiaohongshu Press. November 2023.</p>
          <p>恢复比修复更具生态效益 | 圣境对话 | 自然圣境微信公众平台 <a href="https://mp.weixin.qq.com/s/mzauyGG6e4BTDcdyzr3Jdw" target="_blank" rel="noopener">“Ecological recovery is better than restoration.”</a> (<em>in Chinese</em>). The Blog of Sacred Earth. June 5, 2023.</p>
          <p><a href="https://www.thepolarisproject.org/curiosity-as-my-guide/" target="_blank" rel="noopener">“Curiosity as my guide.”</a> The Blog of the Woodwell Polaris Project. July 5, 2018.</p>
        </div>
      </div>
      <img class="rounded" src="/uploads/2023/10/Screen-Shot-2023-10-10-at-11.15.33-PM-1.png" alt="" loading="lazy" />
    </section>
  </div>
</Base>
